The '''Giant Mole''' is a simple low-level [[boss]] that can be found under [[Falador]]. It is killed for its [[mole claw]], [[mole skin]], [[immaculate mole skin]], and [[Baby Mole]] drops.

==Suggested skills==
*{{SCP|Attack|60+}}
*{{SCP|Strength|60+}}
*{{SCP|Defence|60+}} 
*{{SCP|Hitpoints|60+}}
*{{SCP|Ranged|60+}} (If using ranged)
*{{SCP|Magic|60+}} (If using magic)
*{{SCP|Prayer|43+}} for [[Protect from Melee]] (44+ [[Eagle Eye]], 70+ [[Piety]], 74+ [[Rigour]])

==Transportation==
{{Map|2984,3387|2987,3387|2999,3375|2996,3377|3005,3376|2989,3378|plane=0|mapID=0|mtype=dot|align=right|caption=The location of the [[Mole hill|mole hills]] in [[Falador Park]].}}
The [[Giant Mole]] is located in the [[Mole Hole]] under [[Falador]]. The entrance point is located at [[Falador Park]], where there are [[Mole hill|mole hills]] scattered on the west side. The closest teleport is the [[Falador Park]] option(3) on the [[Ring of wealth|ring of wealth]]. Players must bring a [[spade]] to dig underground and a [[light source]] of some type is required or they will be constantly bitten by bugs. A [[Fire of Eternal Light]] can be lit inside the cave after completing the [[Making Friends with My Arm]] quest which provides permanent light inside the cave.

In the north-west of Falador park is a mole hill with a spade. This allows access to a private instance of the mole hill for 25000 gp.  Players who have completed the Hard tier Combat Achievements will receive a reduced price of 12,500 GP. Also, the price is halved for Ironman accounts, reducing the cost to either 12,500 GP or 6,250 GP for those who have completed the Hard Combat Achievements.

==Attacks and abilities==
*[[Melee]] attack: The [[Giant Mole|mole]] swipes a claw at its target, dealing up to 21 damage.
*Burrow: When the mole's health is between 5-50%, there is a 25% chance for any incoming attack to cause it to burrow away into another location.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1139454530406559744|date=14 June 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107093|archivedate=18 June 2019|quote=1/4 when its health is between 5% and 50%.}} There is also a chance that the dirt she digs while burrowing to escape can extinguish the player's [[light source]] (shown with dirt splatters on the player's screen), though covered light sources will be unaffected by this. Note that splashed magic attacks cannot trigger her to dig, making weapons such as the [[Tumeken's shadow|Tumeken's Shadow]] particularly good for fighting the mole.

==Guide==
[[File:Giant Mole Cannon Location.png|thumb|Cannon double hit spot when using the western safespot at the centre of the cave.]]
Combat with the [[Giant Mole|mole]] is straightforward, as it doesn't have any unique attacks or abilities that can endanger the player.

For low levelled players, the mole can be [[safespotted]] with many of the cavern walls. [[Maging]] with earth spells is highly recommended when safespotting. The mole has 50% elemental weakness to earth spells, and splashes cannot trigger the mole to dig. Players [[meleeing]] it  should activate [[Protect from Melee]] and use [[stab]] weapons, as it has lower stab defence compared to [[slash]] and [[crush]].

For high levelled players, the mole can be killed quickly with [[Dharok the Wretched's equipment]], as it is easily possible to kill her within 2-3 hits depending on the player's strength boosting equipment. Simply lower your health to 1 with the [[Locator orb]] or [[Dwarven rock cake]], activate [[Protect from Melee]] and flick [[Piety]].

When the mole reaches half health and lower, there is a chance that it will dig away to another location in the lair. Without the [[Falador shield 3]] or [[Falador shield 4|4]], it can be a tedious task, as players may have to navigate through the whole lair to find the mole. The mole also loses [[aggression]] towards the primary target when burrowing away. [[Thrall]]s can be used as a makeshift substitute for the Falador shield, as they will begin to path towards the mole's new location after she digs in order to attack her, but as thrall's max hit is 3 and they can make the giant mole dig, this is not recommended.

Completion of the hard [[Falador diaries]] is highly recommended, as players with the shield can locate the mole whenever it digs away. It also notes the 100% drop of [[mole skin]] and [[Mole claw|claws]], prolonging trips.

Poison is a fantastic tool against the Mole, since she will not burrow from poison damage, significantly shortening kill times. For [[ironmen]] (who may not have access to [[Poison(++)]] potions due to the high Herblore requirement), a great alternative is completing the [[Tai Bwo Wannai Trio]] quest and speaking to [[Tamayu]], who will reward the player with a [[rune spear (kp)]]. This karambwan-poison-coated weapon has the same poison strength as Poison(++).

